e  as much and um  at the moment i feel like all of that is  behind us and that you know despite all  the obstacles that we faced we finally  reached this day through campaigning and  through his own sacrifices because he  he did sacrifice his health his safety  to send out recordings from prison  through covet to  you know display the horrible conditions  that were happening in prison he sent  recordings afterwards begging you know  boris johnson and the foreign  ministry to help him and the other  prisoners and he's campaigned for  everyone who is detained there so i  think the sacrifices have paid off and  you know  we can't  undo what's been done but we  have learned a lot from this we've grown  from this and hopefully we're going to  use that now to  to campaign and help  everyone else that's been um  behind you know left behind in iran or  for any future families that this might  happen to to may be able to prevent it  it's fantastic news and it's great to  share your relief and your celebration  that's him coming home  what kind of man is he and and is he  someone who will be  campaigning for those he's left behind  will you be as well or do you want to  just draw a line under it because of  course there are lots of other well  there are a number of other iranian  british nationals and others who are  incarcerated still we don't know their  names they haven't done what you've done  to campaign to get them out their  families  but there are a lot left aren't there  who are still languishing in jail  there are not just british other  nationalities as well obviously  uh i'm i'm  beyond 100  certain that once initiate goes through  a brief period of recuperating and  actually finding himself  and uh adjusting to everyday life even i  mean you can imagine even social media  you know internet changes over the past  years have been great once he adjusts  himself he will go  full force into campaigning for others  and  trying to help those left behind as you  said most definitely yeah and not only  him like we have made very strong  connections with the families of the  other detainees so uh we feel like it's  our responsibility  to  be their voice because uh we have  succeeded in our journey but there are  people who are still where we were  yesterday and they don't know how long  they're going to be  on that journey of suffering and  frustration so we would do our utmost to  help those people as well because they  are our friends at the end of the day  and looking forward to your  recovery as a family what does that look  like for you in the days and the weeks  that follow  honestly we've missed doing so many  ordinary things together you know we've  missed birthdays we've missed  christmases  we've missed walking the dog uh taking a  simple holiday  you know sitting together drinking a cup  of coffee just walking hand in hand  walking in our local park  all of this  is is we have to start all over again  we have to pick up life where it was  left off very  abruptly  and  just try and  try and find a semblance of the life  that  we had sort of been unhired us from for  the past five years  and and sherry just very briefly what  did you feel when you saw those pictures  of your husband touching down in muskats  um how does it make you feel  honestly i i think even until then i  couldn't quite  get my head around the fact that he was  he was flying and he was on his way here  there have been so many obstacles that  uh your mind puts this that you put you  have this mental break on you don't want  to admit to yourself that it's happening  but i think as we get closer to the time  that they land it's sinking in more and  more and uh  it's  overwhelming it's uh it's it's very  difficult to describe  okay  very deep joy yeah sherry and ali kazuri  thank you so much for  joining us on sky news and donek wagon  thank you for your insights as well  today
 

